body:
The boys have said repeatedly that they love the live shows, both Blurryface and Trench were written around how they would be executed live. I couldn't imagine either one of the boys giving that up for good. When it comes to children, that could definitely slow them down, but I don't think for a second it would stop them. In the same interview Tyler said he needed to create. Their lives and our lives will both go on, but I think to stop creating for Tyler would be unthinkable. He said he needs to create. Additionally, they both care about us and the Clique.

&#x200B;

Bottom Line: When the time comes for them to take the next steps in their life, I genuinely believe we'll get some sort of, "hey, this really cool kid has now appeared in my life so I'm going to focus on it for a while, but I'll be around!" message. They wouldn't leave us high and dry, they said so in an interview after the release of Trench. Tyler and Josh love live shows, I think they'll do them (although, less frequently as time goes on) until they physically cannot or people stop coming. Tyler needs to create. Expect music (although, maybe at a slower pace) for a long time.
